FUN_1000_3436 / FUN_1000_3446 (post-driver free-list builder): DGROUP near-offset list as host pointers.

Reached from app_entry right after the 0x5200 driver-processing (FUN_1000_5228) completes.  FUN_1000_3436
falls through into FUN_1000_3446 (Ghidra duplicated the shared tail into both C functions).  asm 0x13446
builds a 0x3f-node free list in DGROUP from offset 0x18ea (each node 0x12 bytes, [node]=next-offset,
0xffff-terminated) then calls FUN_1000_46b6(0x3e0b).  The list pointers are DGROUP NEAR OFFSETS, but Ghidra
typed them as host `undefined2 *` (&DAT_1000_d8ea ...) with host-pointer arithmetic (puVar1+9), producing
wrong link values and a bad-pointer store SIGSEGV.  Reconstruct both copies with 16-bit near offsets based
at g_mem+DGROUP.  The leading `lcall [DGROUP:0x12]` reloc apply has bx=0 so the engine f842 bails
immediately (kept verbatim).  Asm-verified base-0 0x13446..0x13484.
